  partName: Sensor
  description: The Sensor is a tiny, compact component situated at the top-center-rear
    of the engine, made of Material.001, and plays a crucial role in monitoring various
    engine parameters, such as temperature, pressure, or flow rates. Its primary
    function is to provide vital data to the engine control unit, enabling it to
    adjust engine settings and optimize performance. An interesting aspect of the
    Sensor is its ability to operate accurately in a wide range of temperatures and
    environmental conditions, making it a reliable and essential component for modern
    engine management systems.
